---
layout: base.njk
title: Apuntes
description: Apuntes de estudio de mis cursos, con figuras interactivas.
permalink: /es/notes/
scripts:
  - /assets/js/notes-index.js
---
{%- from "macros.njk" import langSwitch -%}
{%- set other = page.url | otherLanguage(collections.all) -%}
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Apuntes</h1>
    <p>Apuntes de estudio de mis cursos, con figuras interactivas para explorar.</p>
    {%- if other %}
    <p class="page-lang">{{ langSwitch(other, "es") }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </header>

  {#- Courses in the order set by `courseOrder` in each course folder's JSON file, each one opened and closed by the
      reader, so that a long list of courses stays short until one is opened. #}
  <div class="courses">
    {%- for course in collections.notesEs | courses %}
    {%- set notes = collections.notesEs | byCourse(course) %}
    <details class="course" id="{{ course | slugify }}">
      <summary>
        <h2>{{ course }}</h2>
        <span class="count">{{ notes.length }} {{ "apunte" if notes.length == 1 else "apuntes" }}</span>
        <svg class="toggle" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h10"/><path class="v" d="M8 3v10"/></svg>
      </summary>
      {#- A table of contents: the notes are read in order, so they are numbered, in runs that share a module, which is
          named once beside its run. #}
      {%- for group in notes | moduleGroups %}
      <div class="toc-group">
        <h3>{{ group.module }}</h3>
        <ol class="toc" role="list">
          {%- for note in group.notes %}
          <li>
            <span class="n">{{ group.start + loop.index0 }}</span>
            <div><a href="{{ note.url }}">{{ note.data.title }}</a><p>{{ note.data.description }}</p></div>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </details>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <p class="notice">Son apuntes personales de estudio, escritos con ayuda de IA. Pueden contener errores.</p>
</div>
